is of S. aureus."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Bacteriology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a7bef0ca235b","stem":"Which of the following statements is FALSE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"An example of 0assive humoral immunity is treatment with horse anti-snace venin."},{"label":"B","text":"Antigen recognized by helper T cells must be associated with Class II MHC molecules on the surface of professional APC"},{"label":"C","text":"Each lymphocyte has many antigen binding receptnrs, each receptor capable of binding the sole antigen. d* Recognition and killing of virus-infected cells by cytotoxic T cells is an example of adaptive immunity."},{"label":"E","text":"The innate immune system does not deal with endogenous antigen. QUESTIONS ON ANTIGENS:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ddd53843a7c3208057acb162a2c5585b42e5b16c"},{"id":"q-f9fb24300162","stem":"The ability of an antigen to induce an immune response does NOT depend on the antigen's","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"ability to enter the thyroid."},{"label":"B","text":"degree of aggregation."},{"label":"C","text":"dose."},{"label":"D","text":"size."},{"label":"E","text":"usual presence in the body."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ae07142d5212","stem":"Alum is an effective adjuvant because it","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"disaggregates the antigen."},{"label":"B","text":"is immunogenic for stem cells"},{"label":"C","text":"is immunogenic for T cells."},{"label":"D","text":"slows the release of antigen."},{"label":"E","text":"transports antigen into the cytoplasm of antigen-presenting cells."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f98bac530b29","stem":"Antibody cross-reactivity is demonstrated by antibody binding to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"a cell surface marker."},{"label":"B","text":"a hapten."},{"label":"C","text":"a hapten-carrier complex."},{"label":"D","text":"an antigen that is structurally similar to the immunogen"},{"label":"E","text":"the immunogen."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswe