,"stem":"Rearrangement of both TCR and BCR gene segments does NOT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"generate diversity of antigen binding by recombination of a large pool of germline V, D, and J segments."},{"label":"B","text":"lead to CDR3 being the most hypervariable region in the receptor chains."},{"label":"C","text":"require RAG-1, RAG-2, and TdT expression."},{"label":"D","text":"result in allelic exclusion of membrane receptors."},{"label":"E","text":"result in isotype switching after antigen stimulation of the mature lymphocytes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-03082b3a2571","stem":"The amount of diversity in TCR generated within one individual by somatic recombination","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"is higher than BCR diversity."},{"label":"B","text":"is about the same as for BCR diversity."},{"label":"C","text":"is lower than BCR diversity."},{"label":"D","text":"is lower than Class I MHC diversity."},{"label":"E","text":"is lower than Class II MHC diversity."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3b825794f713","stem":"T cells use all of the following for generating antigen-recognition diversity on the TCR, except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"combinatorial association of chains."},{"label":"B","text":"combinatorial association of segments."},{"label":"C","text":"large germline pool of gene sequences."},{"label":"D","text":"N region addition of nucleotides."},{"label":"E","text":"somatic hypermutation."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-128b05f515cf","stem":"CD8 is a co-receptor on T cells that binds","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"CD3."},{"label":"B","text":"endogenous antigen peptide."},{"label":"C","text":"the constant region of Class I MHC."},{"label":"D","text":"the constant region of TCR."},{"label":"E","text":"the variable region of Class I MHC."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-6b136e22156a","stem":"All of the following are true for antigen receptors on both B cells and T cells EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"associated with signal transduction molecules in the membrane."},{"label":"B","text":"generated by somatic recombination during lymphocyte development."},{"label":"C","text":"members of the Ig gene superfamily."},{"label":"D","text":"MHC-restricted in their ability to bind antigen."},{"label":"E","text":"specific for a single antigen epitope."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-71d6f3c06c79","stem":"Which of the following statements is FALSE?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Microorganisms and Infection","topicOriginal":"Microorganisms and Infection","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"TCR is allelically excluded on individual T cells."},{"label":"B","text":"CD4 and CD8 co-receptors are also signal transducing molecules for T cell activation."},{"label":"C","text":"The arrangement of α chain gene segments most closely resembles that of κ chain."},{"label":"D","text":"The gene segments for the δ chain are interspersed with those for the γ chain."},{"label":"E","text":"The T cells that are most likely to react against allogeneic kidney cells are CD8+ cytotoxic T cells. Problems"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Microorganisms and Infection","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"dupl