"label":"C","text":"A set of data selected from a larger set of data."},{"label":"D","text":"A decision, estimate, prediction or generalization about sample based on information contained in a population."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"232a0dfac95293f2443be08d2c5a013ee8f0342c"},{"id":"q-87822850a24f","stem":"Read the table below and look at the P value. In each case, think about what the P value tells you, and what the confidence interval for the mean difference tells you. [pic]","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Biostatistics","topicOriginal":"Biostatistics","subtopic":"Statistical Inference","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The mean systolic blood pressure is statistically significant"},{"label":"B","text":"There is statistically significant observed mean difference between the systolic and diastolic blood pressure"},{"label":"C","text":"A and B are correct"},{"label":"D","text":"None is correct"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Biostatistics","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8111858bbb78","stem":"Given that mean = 12, total number of observation = 132, then the number of observation/frequency will be","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"op