opulation) Inclusion and exclusion criteria Sampling process or procedure? Tools & procedures How did they collect the information? Interviews? Clinical observation? Check list? Variables Main outcome? Independent variables? Data analysis plan/ methods? Data summarization for continuous and categorical? How did they measure the associations?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Biostatistics and Research","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Biostatistics and Research","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-abd6f9c8f6d1","stem":"Study design used in detail how did they define cases? were the cases prevalent or incident cases? were they selected at hospital or at the community? were they representatives? Was it through interviews or records or clinical examination? How did they measure the exposure?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Cases;"},{"label":"B","text":"Controls; who/how did they define controls?, source of controls, hospitals or at other places, what was the ratio of cases: controls"},{"label":"C","text":"Was it a matched or unmatched case-control study?"},{"label":"D","text":"How did they collect exposure information?"},{"label":"E","text":"How did they ascertain cases?"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-41a00696b4c3","stem":"Measures of association usually used with the design you have mentioned from the paper? Do the measures match the design?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6003ff7e0db2","stem":"Did the result section reflect the objectives of the study in this paper?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e8859cf30b86","stem":"Main conclusion of the paper. Did it match the objectives?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags