:"D","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2ac830d9270364de6b4c6e3aa97c78949681e5e6"},{"id":"q-8b275f2be879","stem":"Researchers use both open-ended and closed-ended questions to collect data. Which of the following statements is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"Epidemiology","subtopic":"Epidemiolog","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Open-ended questions directly provide quantitative data based on the researcher’s predetermined response categories 8"},{"label":"B","text":"Closed-ended questions provide quantitative data in the participant’s own words"},{"label":"C","text":"Open-ended questions provide qualitative data in the participant’s own words"},{"label":"D","text":"Closed-ended questions directly provide qualitative data in the participants’ own words"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Community Health and Public Health","displayTopic":"Epidemiology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"da025bac73eac172f6f3511fb805833fa515b98a"},{"id":"q-8c039d7c9c99","stem":"Which of the following will give a more “accurate” representation of the population from which a sample has been taken?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Community Health and Public Health","topic":"Epidemiology","topicOriginal":"E